{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q018_tal_effector_repeat_lengths\",\"answer\":\"They share a homologous repeat unit, not a fixed total length. In SCOPe 2.08, the genetic-style SEQRES domain sequences are 51 residues for d2kq5a_ (PthA), 373 for d3v6pa_ (dHax3), and 752 for d4cj9a_ (BurrH). These structures contain different extents of the TAL-like repeat architecture; repeat copy number and construct boundaries can vary without changing family membership. SCOPe explicitly annotates d2kq5a_ as “single repeat” and marks d2kq5a_ and d3v6pa_ with “re,” indicating differing numbers of small repeating units within a family.\\n\\nAll three belong to family a.298.1.1, TAL (transcription activator-like) effector (SUNID 267609), within superfamily a.298.1, TAL effector-like; fold a.298, Left-handed alpha-alpha superhelix; and class a, All alpha proteins. Family membership supports a close evolutionary relationship of the repeat architecture; the superfamily expresses broader homology, whereas fold and class alone describe structural similarity without establishing common ancestry.\\n\\nSCOPe identifies 4cj9 A:259–292, a 34-residue segment, as the canonical representative repeat. Those coordinates apply to d4cj9a_, not directly to either other domain, and do not delimit the entire BurrH domain. Total lengths should not simply be divided by 34 to assign exact repeat counts. A single-repeat structure can inform local repeat geometry but cannot by itself template an entire array or its overall conformation. Shared family membership also does not establish identical DNA specificity or transcriptional activity: transferring those properties requires repeat-level sequence analysis, structural context, and functional evidence.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"Pretrained protein structural-classification knowledge\",\"mcp__scope__get_scop_domains\",\"mcp__scope__get_scop_sequence\",\"/api/v1/releases/current\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d2kq5a_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3v6pa_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/parents\",\"/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d4cj9a_/annotations\",\"/api/v1/sequences/sids/d2kq5a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\",\"/api/v1/sequences/sids/d3v6pa_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\",\"/api/v1/sequences/sids/d4cj9a_?release=2.08&source=seqres&style=genetic&format=json\"]}]}"}}
